{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794531672284,"sessionID":"ses_e2d947600ffedS5gf0ax58bCAA","part":{"partID":"prt_1d26c40bb002cbpKGBUNSGtxnC","sessionID":"ses_e2d947600ffedS5gf0ax58bCAA","messageID":"msg_1d26c38b90010ayxkEK6fXxMOu","type":"tool","id":"call_24f73e65f787428698f1ad69","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md, lines 1-222\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\"\n3: description: \"Ordered tasks to add the Gate 2 command bullet, copy it into the Cursor rule, hand hub modes to their commands, name the plan workflow at Gate 3 and downgrade commands in a child brief.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"gate 2 binding and runtime pointers tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: \n26: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n27: \n28: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `SSK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime`. `SYNC` is `$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`. `MAN` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`. `CHK` is `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs`. `HOOKDOC` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`. `S` is this phase's `scratch/` folder. `G1T` is `(cd $SSK/cli && npx vitest run tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts --config ../vitest.config.ts --root .)`.\n29: \n30: Each task is one change to the files it names, small enough for a worker with a short brief. The operator answered the four wording questions on 2026-11-12, and `spec.md` section 10 quotes each answer. No task reads holdout prompt text.\n31: \n32: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel.\n33: - Wave 0, 2 tasks: T001, T002. Read-only setup.\n34: - Wave 1, 12 tasks: T003 (`AGENTS.md`), T004 (`SYNC`), T005 (`HOOKDOC`), T006 (`advisor-runtime-values.ts`), T007 (`advisor-observability.vitest.ts`), T008 (`hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`), T009, T010 and T011 (one `ROUTER.md` each), T012 (`spec-gate-core.mjs`), T013 (`create.sh`), T014 (the deriver, only if its condition holds).\n35: - Wave 2, 8 tasks: T015 (`render.ts`), T016 (`MAN`), T017 (gate1 test), T018 (`HOOKDOC`), T019 (parity test, new), T020 (spec-gate test), T021 (runtime-mirrors README), T022 (label removal test, new).\n36: - Wave 3, 4 tasks: T023 (child render test, new), T024 (`MAN`, generated), T025 (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, generated), T026 (`HOOKDOC`).\n37: - Verification, 9 tasks, one at a time: T027 to T035.\n38: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n39: \n40: ---\n41: \n42: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n43: ## Phase 1: Setup\n44: \n45: - [x] T001 Re-read the before numbers (`$S/before.txt`). Verify: `$CHK | grep -E \"^A(4|6) |^STATUS\"` prints `44 current`, `15629 of 16384` and `STATUS=OK`, `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` prints `30 pins`, `node $SYNC --check` exits 0 and `node $S/measure-policies.mjs | head -1` prints `commands 44 {\"start\":20,\"ask\":17,\"run\":7}`.\n46: - [x] T002 Confirm phase 005 shipped the brief line (`$S/phase005-check.txt`). Verify: `bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"create a readme for the utils folder\"` prints a line holding `/create:readme` and `(start)`. If it does not, mark T014, T015, T023, T026 and T033 `[B]` with the line it printed, and carry on with the rest.\n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n52: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n53: \n54: - [ ] T003 Insert one line in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, right after the line `- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed`. The line is the exact content of `$S/bullet-draft.txt`: ``- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]` `` (`AGENTS.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, and `diff <(rg \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\" AGENTS.md) $S/bullet-draft.txt` prints nothing.\n55: - [ ] T004 In `SYNC`, add a second block. Add the constants `START_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:start -->'`, `END_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:end -->'`, `GATE_TWO_CALL_MARKER = 'skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend'` and `GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'`. Read the first `AGENTS.md` line holding each marker, with a leading `2. ` stripped as `readGateOneLine` does. When both lines exist, write a block right after the Gate 1 block: the start marker, `## Gate 2 command routing (generated from the root AGENTS.md)`, a blank line, `Cursor gets no per-prompt advisor brief under the tested build. Before acting, run the direct call below, then apply the command rule:`, a blank line, the call line, a blank line, the command line, a blank line, the same `Generated by` line as block one, the end marker. When either line is missing, remove an existing second block and write nothing for it. Under `--check`, report `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` or `no Gate 2 command block` and exit 1. Export the new names (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`). Verify: `node --check $SYNC` exits 0, and `rg -c \"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '\\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*'\" $SYNC` prints 1.\n56: - [ ] T005 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 3, add a DSH row after the OpenCode row: runtime `**DSH**`, adapter `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs`, wiring `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false`, payload note `A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief`, delivery `Brief added to the step`. In section 4, add a `dsh/` entry with `README.md` and `prompt-advisor.mjs` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n '^\\| \\*\\*DSH\\*\\* \\|' $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c \"prompt-advisor.mjs\" $HOOKDOC` prints at least 2.\n57: - [ ] T006 [P] Remove the `'copilot',` line from `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`, leaving seven labels in this order: `claude`, `opencode`, `pi`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin`, `dsh`. Add no retired list (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts` prints nothing and exits 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0.\n58: - [ ] T007 [P] In the observability test, change the expectation `expect(ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES).toEqual([...])` to the seven labels T006 leaves, in the same order (`$ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, and `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` prints nothing.\n59: - [ ] T008 [P] In the brief benchmark, delete the `copilot` row of `SEVEN_AXIS_MATRIX` and drop `copilot` from the header comment that lists the runtimes (`$ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` prints nothing and exits 1. The bench sits outside `npm run typecheck` and the default test run, so this grep is its check.\n60: - [ ] T009 [P] Add one bullet as the last item of section 4, HOW TO READ THIS, in `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`: ``- A mode whose `mode-registry.json` row names a `command` has two whole entries: read that command's document in full and follow it under the policy the advisor names, or follow this mode's packet. Pick one and keep to it. A mode whose row has `command: null` has only its packet.`` (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-doc` exits 0.\n61: - [ ] T010 [P] Add the same bullet as T009 as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` (`.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-design` exits 0.\n62: - [ ] T011 [P] Add the T009 bullet as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`, followed in the same bullet by: ``Where a mode packet names its command as its only entry, as `deep-research/SKILL.md` does, both entries lead to the command.`` (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop` exits 0.\n63: - [ ] T012 [P] In `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, insert one array item right after `'The answer holds for the rest of this session: do not ask this again on later turns.'`: `'For a new folder, start /speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete when the operator asked for the build itself: read that command document in full and follow it without :auto.'` (`$SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs`). Verify: `rg -c \"speckit:plan\" $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` prints 1, and `node --check $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` exits 0.\n64: - [ ] T013 [P] In the standard next-steps block of `create.sh`, the one that prints `1. Fill out spec.md with requirements`, add after the lazy add-ons `if` block: `echo \"    6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan, or plan and build with /speckit:complete, unless one of them created this folder\"` (`$SSK/cli/spec/create.sh`). Verify: `bash -n $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` exits 0, and `rg -c \"6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan\" $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` prints 1.\n65: - [ ] T014 The command table phase 005 generates (`COMMAND_ROWS` in `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`) carries a policy but no `mutating` class, and T015 needs the class. In `renderCommandRows` of `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`, add `mutating: '<class>'` to each `COMMAND_ROWS` row, taken from the same `commandPolicies` record that supplies the row's policy, placed after `policy` and left out when the row has no policy record. In `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, add `readonly mutating?: 'read-only' | 'add-only' | 'mutates';` to the `CommandRow` interface, outside the generated block. Then run `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`. Verify: `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \"'command-doctor-git-setup': \\{ command: '/doctor:git setup', policy: 'run', mutating: 'read-only'\" $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` prints 1, `rg -c \"'command-doctor-speckit': \\{ command: '/doctor:speckit', policy: 'run', mutating: 'add-only'\" $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` prints 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0 and `npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n66: - [ ] T015 In `$ADV/lib/render.ts`, add `childSession?: boolean` to `AdvisorBriefRenderOptions`, defaulting to `process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1'`. When it is true, the command shown in the head line, and in an `Also:` line, renders `(parent-named only)` in place of its policy word when the policy is `start` or `ask`, or when it is `run` and the class is not `read-only`. Nothing else in the brief changes (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, and `npx vitest run tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts tests/hooks` reports 0 failed.\n67: - [ ] T016 [P] In `MAN` `pins`, add an entry right after `gate1-lookup`: `\"id\": \"gate2-command\"`, `\"kind\": \"first-occurrence\"`, `\"section\": \"gate-2\"`, `\"texts\": [\"**Command in the brief.**\"]`, `\"consumer\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs\"`, `\"consumer_evidence\": [\"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'\"]` and a `why` saying the Cursor rule's second block is generated from the first line holding this marker (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`). Verify: `node -e 'const m=require(\"./.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json\");console.log(m.pins.length, m.pins.some((p)=>p.id===\"gate2-command\"))'` prints `31 true`.\n68: - [ ] T017 [P] In `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, seed `AGENTS.md` with a Gate 2 call line and a command line, and add three cases: both blocks are written and `--check` exits 0, a root with no command line gets block one only and a stale second block is removed, and a hand edit inside the second block makes `--check` exit 1 with `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` (`$SSK/cli/tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`). Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n69: - [ ] T018 [P] In `HOOKDOC`, add a subsection `### Starting a surfaced command` at the end of section 3. It says the command document is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`, the model reads it in full and follows it on every runtime, never tells the user to type a slash command and asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file. Then a table with columns `Runtime`, `Model can start a command itself` and `Basis`, one row each for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, OpenCode and DSH, taken from section 2.8 of `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md`. Write runtime names in plain text, not bold, so the parity test reads only the adapter table. Claude Code's row says the Skill tool is a shortcut for the names it lists, and that it lists one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"^### Starting a surfaced command\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c '^\\| \\*\\*' $HOOKDOC` still prints 7.\n70: - [ ] T019 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`. Export a pure `compareRuntimeLists(index, table, enumValues)` that returns the names missing from each list. Read the index as the directory names under `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/`, the table as the lowercased bold names in `HOOKDOC` rows matching `^\\| \\*\\*([A-Za-z]+)\\*\\* \\|`, and the enum as `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. One case asserts the three real lists agree. One case passes an index with an extra name and asserts the function reports it (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` reports 2 passed and 0 failed.\n71: - [ ] T020 [P] In the test `Gate-3 delivery flag off preserves byte-identical baseline output`, add the T012 line to the `mutationNotice` array at the same position (`$SSK/tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs`). Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0` and `pass 107`.\n72: - [ ] T021 [P] In the `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` row of the runtime-mirrors README, say the script writes two blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`: the Gate 1 lookup and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct call (`$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"sync-gate1-pointers\" $SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md` prints a line naming `Gate 2`.\n73: - [ ] T022 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` for a record or input that still carries `copilot`. Use a temporary workspace root and delete the two files it writes afterwards. Cases: a diagnostics file at `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root)` holding one valid `claude` record and one otherwise valid `copilot` record makes `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords(root)` return only the `claude` record without throwing. The same holds for an outcomes file at `advisorHookOutcomesPath(root)` and `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords(root)`. `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` throws for a `copilot` record. `validateSkillExecutionOutcomeRecord` returns false for one. `AdvisorValidateInputSchema.safeParse` fails for an `outcomeEvents` entry with `runtime: 'copilot'` and names that path in its issues (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` reports 5 passed and 0 failed.\n74: - [ ] T023 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`. Cases, each rendering one result through `renderAdvisorBrief`: child set and policy `start`, `ask`, `run` with `read-only` and `run` with `add-only`, then the variable set to `0` and unset. Expected: `(parent-named only)` for `start`, `ask` and `run` with `add-only`, the policy word for `run` with `read-only`, and output byte-equal to the non-child render for `0` and unset. One more case renders `/doctor:git hooks` as top with the child set (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n75: - [ ] T024 Regenerate the manifest's derived copy (`MAN`). Verify: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` exits 0, then `--check` prints `PASS: 44 sections, 31 pins, derived matches AGENTS.md`.\n76: - [ ] T025 [P] Regenerate the Cursor rule (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`). Verify: `node $SYNC` exits 0, then `node $SYNC --check` exits 0, `rg -c \"Command in the brief\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1 and `rg -c \"skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1.\n77: - [ ] T026 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 2, step 5 Render, add one sentence: with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"parent-named only\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1.\n78: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n83: ## Phase 3: Verification\n84: \n85: - [ ] T027 Run the agents-md check (`$S/after-check.txt`). Verify: `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK`, A4 `44 current`, A5 `31/31 pins hold`, A10 `6/6` and A6 at or under `16384`, expected `16092` with the T003 text unchanged.\n86: - [ ] T028 Run the rule-copy canary. Verify: `node .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/scripts/check-rule-copies.js | head -1` prints a line starting `OK: all rule invariants present`.\n87: - [ ] T029 Run the pointer test and check. Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed, and `node $SYNC --check` exits 0.\n88: - [ ] T030 Run the spec gate test. Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0`.\n89: - [ ] T031 Run the advisor checks. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -n \"copilot\" $ADV --glob \"*.ts\" --glob \"!dist/**\" --glob \"!node_modules/**\"` prints only the new test and the adapter-path guards in `tests/hooks/settings-driven-invocation-parity.vitest.ts` and `stress-test/skill-advisor/hooks-parity-stress.vitest.ts` and `npm test` reports 0 failed.\n90: - [ ] T032 Run the three hub checks. Verify: `for h in sk-doc sk-design system-deep-loop; do node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/$h > /dev/null 2>&1; echo \"$h exit=$?\"; done` prints `exit=0` three times.\n91: - [ ] T033 Rebuild the advisor and probe the hook. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run build` exits 0. Then `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"disable comment hygiene gate\"` prints a line holding `/doctor:git hooks (parent-named only)`, and the same command without the variable prints the phase 005 line with its policy word.\n92: - [ ] T034 Check scope and comment hygiene. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat` names only files in `spec.md` section 3, and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 -- '*.ts' '*.cjs' '*.mjs' '*.sh' | rg \"^\\+.*(REQ-0|T0[0-9]{2}|specs/|ADR-)\"` prints nothing.\n93: - [ ] T035 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n99: ## Completion Criteria\n100: \n101: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n102: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n103: - [ ] `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK` and `node $SYNC --check` exits 0 with the bullet in place\n104: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n109: ## Cross-References\n110: \n111: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n112: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n113: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n114: - **Review**: `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md` R5, R6, R10b, L4, L5, L10, G1 and G3\n115: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: ## Verification Checklist\n120: \n121: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n122: ## Verification Protocol\n123: \n124: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n125: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n126: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n127: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n128: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n129: \n130: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. An A6 reading above 16384 blocks the phase.\n131: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n132: \n133: ---\n134: \n135: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n136: ## Pre-Implementation\n137: \n138: - [x] CHK-001 [P0] The four wording questions have an operator answer, quoted in `spec.md` section 10. Evidence: answered on 2026-11-12 through the question dialog. T003, T006, T012, T013, T015 and T026 follow those answers.\n139: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The before numbers are in `$S/before.txt` (T001).\n140: - [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Phase 005's brief line is confirmed, or the REQ-004 tasks are marked `[B]` (T002).\n141: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n146: ## Code Quality\n147: \n148: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] In `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, and `node --check` exits 0 on `SYNC` and `spec-gate-core.mjs`.\n149: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a requirement or a task id (T034).\n150: - [ ] CHK-012 [P1] `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` is written by `SYNC` only, never by hand (T025).\n151: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The child branch reads the class, never the policy word alone (T015, T023).\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n157: ## Testing Checklist\n158: \n159: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK` with A6 at or under 16384 (T027).\n160: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The pointer test passes 7 cases and `--check` exits 0 (T029).\n161: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The child render test covers every renderer axis in `plan.md` (T023).\n162: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The spec gate test, the parity test and `npm test` in `$ADV` report 0 failed (T030, T031).\n163: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n164: \n165: ---\n166: \n167: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n168: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n169: \n170: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `cross-consumer`: one rule, read by seven runtimes through four surfaces.\n171: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the pointer generator is checked: `rg -l \"sync-gate1-pointers\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists only files this phase changed or confirmed unchanged in `plan.md`.\n172: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Every reader of `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` is checked: `rg -n \"GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE\" .skilled --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists the core, its test and the injection contract, which names it without quoting it.\n173: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The matrix axes in `plan.md` are listed in the two test file headers.\n174: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The child test sets and restores `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, so no other test sees it.\n175: - [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n176: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n177: \n178: ---\n179: \n180: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n181: ## Security\n182: \n183: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] A child never sees a bare `start` or `ask` command line (T023).\n184: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No changed file names `/local-skilled-alignment`: `rg -n \"local-skilled-alignment\" <changed files>` prints nothing.\n185: - [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The pointer block copies tracked `AGENTS.md` text only (T004).\n186: - [ ] CHK-033 [P0] A stored record carrying `copilot` is skipped by both readers without an error, and tool input carrying it is rejected (T022).\n187: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n188: \n189: ---\n190: \n191: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n192: ## Documentation\n193: \n194: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same bullet text, byte count and pin count.\n195: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] `HOOKDOC` names seven adapters and holds the invocation table (T005, T018).\n196: - [ ] CHK-042 [P2] The runtime-mirrors README names both pointer blocks (T021).\n197: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n198: \n199: ---\n200: \n201: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n202: ## File Organization\n203: \n204: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, before and after output live in `scratch/` only.\n205: - [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` holds only the evidence files the summary cites at completion.\n206: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n207: \n208: ---\n209: \n210: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n211: ## Verification Summary\n212: \n213: | Category | Total | Verified |\n214: |----------|-------|----------|\n215: | P0 Items | 13 | 1/13 |\n216: | P1 Items | 12 | 0/12 |\n217: | P2 Items | 1 | 0/1 |\n218: \n219: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-12\n220: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n221: \n222: ---","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md, lines 1-222\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\"\n3: description: \"Ordered tasks to add the Gate 2 command bullet, copy it into the Cursor rule, hand hub modes to their commands, name the plan workflow at Gate 3 and downgrade commands in a child brief.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"gate 2 binding and runtime pointers tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: \n26: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n27: \n28: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `SSK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime`. `SYNC` is `$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`. `MAN` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`. `CHK` is `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs`. `HOOKDOC` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`. `S` is this phase's `scratch/` folder. `G1T` is `(cd $SSK/cli && npx vitest run tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts --config ../vitest.config.ts --root .)`.\n29: \n30: Each task is one change to the files it names, small enough for a worker with a short brief. The operator answered the four wording questions on 2026-11-12, and `spec.md` section 10 quotes each answer. No task reads holdout prompt text.\n31: \n32: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel.\n33: - Wave 0, 2 tasks: T001, T002. Read-only setup.\n34: - Wave 1, 12 tasks: T003 (`AGENTS.md`), T004 (`SYNC`), T005 (`HOOKDOC`), T006 (`advisor-runtime-values.ts`), T007 (`advisor-observability.vitest.ts`), T008 (`hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`), T009, T010 and T011 (one `ROUTER.md` each), T012 (`spec-gate-core.mjs`), T013 (`create.sh`), T014 (the deriver, only if its condition holds).\n35: - Wave 2, 8 tasks: T015 (`render.ts`), T016 (`MAN`), T017 (gate1 test), T018 (`HOOKDOC`), T019 (parity test, new), T020 (spec-gate test), T021 (runtime-mirrors README), T022 (label removal test, new).\n36: - Wave 3, 4 tasks: T023 (child render test, new), T024 (`MAN`, generated), T025 (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, generated), T026 (`HOOKDOC`).\n37: - Verification, 9 tasks, one at a time: T027 to T035.\n38: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n39: \n40: ---\n41: \n42: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n43: ## Phase 1: Setup\n44: \n45: - [x] T001 Re-read the before numbers (`$S/before.txt`). Verify: `$CHK | grep -E \"^A(4|6) |^STATUS\"` prints `44 current`, `15629 of 16384` and `STATUS=OK`, `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` prints `30 pins`, `node $SYNC --check` exits 0 and `node $S/measure-policies.mjs | head -1` prints `commands 44 {\"start\":20,\"ask\":17,\"run\":7}`.\n46: - [x] T002 Confirm phase 005 shipped the brief line (`$S/phase005-check.txt`). Verify: `bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"create a readme for the utils folder\"` prints a line holding `/create:readme` and `(start)`. If it does not, mark T014, T015, T023, T026 and T033 `[B]` with the line it printed, and carry on with the rest.\n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n52: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n53: \n54: - [ ] T003 Insert one line in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, right after the line `- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed`. The line is the exact content of `$S/bullet-draft.txt`: ``- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]` `` (`AGENTS.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, and `diff <(rg \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\" AGENTS.md) $S/bullet-draft.txt` prints nothing.\n55: - [ ] T004 In `SYNC`, add a second block. Add the constants `START_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:start -->'`, `END_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:end -->'`, `GATE_TWO_CALL_MARKER = 'skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend'` and `GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'`. Read the first `AGENTS.md` line holding each marker, with a leading `2. ` stripped as `readGateOneLine` does. When both lines exist, write a block right after the Gate 1 block: the start marker, `## Gate 2 command routing (generated from the root AGENTS.md)`, a blank line, `Cursor gets no per-prompt advisor brief under the tested build. Before acting, run the direct call below, then apply the command rule:`, a blank line, the call line, a blank line, the command line, a blank line, the same `Generated by` line as block one, the end marker. When either line is missing, remove an existing second block and write nothing for it. Under `--check`, report `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` or `no Gate 2 command block` and exit 1. Export the new names (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`). Verify: `node --check $SYNC` exits 0, and `rg -c \"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '\\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*'\" $SYNC` prints 1.\n56: - [ ] T005 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 3, add a DSH row after the OpenCode row: runtime `**DSH**`, adapter `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs`, wiring `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false`, payload note `A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief`, delivery `Brief added to the step`. In section 4, add a `dsh/` entry with `README.md` and `prompt-advisor.mjs` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n '^\\| \\*\\*DSH\\*\\* \\|' $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c \"prompt-advisor.mjs\" $HOOKDOC` prints at least 2.\n57: - [ ] T006 [P] Remove the `'copilot',` line from `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`, leaving seven labels in this order: `claude`, `opencode`, `pi`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin`, `dsh`. Add no retired list (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts` prints nothing and exits 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0.\n58: - [ ] T007 [P] In the observability test, change the expectation `expect(ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES).toEqual([...])` to the seven labels T006 leaves, in the same order (`$ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, and `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` prints nothing.\n59: - [ ] T008 [P] In the brief benchmark, delete the `copilot` row of `SEVEN_AXIS_MATRIX` and drop `copilot` from the header comment that lists the runtimes (`$ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` prints nothing and exits 1. The bench sits outside `npm run typecheck` and the default test run, so this grep is its check.\n60: - [ ] T009 [P] Add one bullet as the last item of section 4, HOW TO READ THIS, in `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`: ``- A mode whose `mode-registry.json` row names a `command` has two whole entries: read that command's document in full and follow it under the policy the advisor names, or follow this mode's packet. Pick one and keep to it. A mode whose row has `command: null` has only its packet.`` (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-doc` exits 0.\n61: - [ ] T010 [P] Add the same bullet as T009 as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` (`.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-design` exits 0.\n62: - [ ] T011 [P] Add the T009 bullet as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`, followed in the same bullet by: ``Where a mode packet names its command as its only entry, as `deep-research/SKILL.md` does, both entries lead to the command.`` (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop` exits 0.\n63: - [ ] T012 [P] In `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, insert one array item right after `'The answer holds for the rest of this session: do not ask this again on later turns.'`: `'For a new folder, start /speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete when the operator asked for the build itself: read that command document in full and follow it without :auto.'` (`$SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs`). Verify: `rg -c \"speckit:plan\" $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` prints 1, and `node --check $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` exits 0.\n64: - [ ] T013 [P] In the standard next-steps block of `create.sh`, the one that prints `1. Fill out spec.md with requirements`, add after the lazy add-ons `if` block: `echo \"    6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan, or plan and build with /speckit:complete, unless one of them created this folder\"` (`$SSK/cli/spec/create.sh`). Verify: `bash -n $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` exits 0, and `rg -c \"6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan\" $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` prints 1.\n65: - [ ] T014 The command table phase 005 generates (`COMMAND_ROWS` in `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`) carries a policy but no `mutating` class, and T015 needs the class. In `renderCommandRows` of `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`, add `mutating: '<class>'` to each `COMMAND_ROWS` row, taken from the same `commandPolicies` record that supplies the row's policy, placed after `policy` and left out when the row has no policy record. In `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, add `readonly mutating?: 'read-only' | 'add-only' | 'mutates';` to the `CommandRow` interface, outside the generated block. Then run `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`. Verify: `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \"'command-doctor-git-setup': \\{ command: '/doctor:git setup', policy: 'run', mutating: 'read-only'\" $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` prints 1, `rg -c \"'command-doctor-speckit': \\{ command: '/doctor:speckit', policy: 'run', mutating: 'add-only'\" $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` prints 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0 and `npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n66: - [ ] T015 In `$ADV/lib/render.ts`, add `childSession?: boolean` to `AdvisorBriefRenderOptions`, defaulting to `process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1'`. When it is true, the command shown in the head line, and in an `Also:` line, renders `(parent-named only)` in place of its policy word when the policy is `start` or `ask`, or when it is `run` and the class is not `read-only`. Nothing else in the brief changes (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, and `npx vitest run tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts tests/hooks` reports 0 failed.\n67: - [ ] T016 [P] In `MAN` `pins`, add an entry right after `gate1-lookup`: `\"id\": \"gate2-command\"`, `\"kind\": \"first-occurrence\"`, `\"section\": \"gate-2\"`, `\"texts\": [\"**Command in the brief.**\"]`, `\"consumer\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs\"`, `\"consumer_evidence\": [\"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'\"]` and a `why` saying the Cursor rule's second block is generated from the first line holding this marker (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`). Verify: `node -e 'const m=require(\"./.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json\");console.log(m.pins.length, m.pins.some((p)=>p.id===\"gate2-command\"))'` prints `31 true`.\n68: - [ ] T017 [P] In `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, seed `AGENTS.md` with a Gate 2 call line and a command line, and add three cases: both blocks are written and `--check` exits 0, a root with no command line gets block one only and a stale second block is removed, and a hand edit inside the second block makes `--check` exit 1 with `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` (`$SSK/cli/tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`). Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n69: - [ ] T018 [P] In `HOOKDOC`, add a subsection `### Starting a surfaced command` at the end of section 3. It says the command document is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`, the model reads it in full and follows it on every runtime, never tells the user to type a slash command and asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file. Then a table with columns `Runtime`, `Model can start a command itself` and `Basis`, one row each for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, OpenCode and DSH, taken from section 2.8 of `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md`. Write runtime names in plain text, not bold, so the parity test reads only the adapter table. Claude Code's row says the Skill tool is a shortcut for the names it lists, and that it lists one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"^### Starting a surfaced command\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c '^\\| \\*\\*' $HOOKDOC` still prints 7.\n70: - [ ] T019 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`. Export a pure `compareRuntimeLists(index, table, enumValues)` that returns the names missing from each list. Read the index as the directory names under `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/`, the table as the lowercased bold names in `HOOKDOC` rows matching `^\\| \\*\\*([A-Za-z]+)\\*\\* \\|`, and the enum as `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. One case asserts the three real lists agree. One case passes an index with an extra name and asserts the function reports it (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` reports 2 passed and 0 failed.\n71: - [ ] T020 [P] In the test `Gate-3 delivery flag off preserves byte-identical baseline output`, add the T012 line to the `mutationNotice` array at the same position (`$SSK/tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs`). Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0` and `pass 107`.\n72: - [ ] T021 [P] In the `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` row of the runtime-mirrors README, say the script writes two blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`: the Gate 1 lookup and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct call (`$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"sync-gate1-pointers\" $SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md` prints a line naming `Gate 2`.\n73: - [ ] T022 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` for a record or input that still carries `copilot`. Use a temporary workspace root and delete the two files it writes afterwards. Cases: a diagnostics file at `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root)` holding one valid `claude` record and one otherwise valid `copilot` record makes `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords(root)` return only the `claude` record without throwing. The same holds for an outcomes file at `advisorHookOutcomesPath(root)` and `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords(root)`. `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` throws for a `copilot` record. `validateSkillExecutionOutcomeRecord` returns false for one. `AdvisorValidateInputSchema.safeParse` fails for an `outcomeEvents` entry with `runtime: 'copilot'` and names that path in its issues (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` reports 5 passed and 0 failed.\n74: - [ ] T023 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`. Cases, each rendering one result through `renderAdvisorBrief`: child set and policy `start`, `ask`, `run` with `read-only` and `run` with `add-only`, then the variable set to `0` and unset. Expected: `(parent-named only)` for `start`, `ask` and `run` with `add-only`, the policy word for `run` with `read-only`, and output byte-equal to the non-child render for `0` and unset. One more case renders `/doctor:git hooks` as top with the child set (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n75: - [ ] T024 Regenerate the manifest's derived copy (`MAN`). Verify: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` exits 0, then `--check` prints `PASS: 44 sections, 31 pins, derived matches AGENTS.md`.\n76: - [ ] T025 [P] Regenerate the Cursor rule (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`). Verify: `node $SYNC` exits 0, then `node $SYNC --check` exits 0, `rg -c \"Command in the brief\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1 and `rg -c \"skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1.\n77: - [ ] T026 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 2, step 5 Render, add one sentence: with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"parent-named only\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1.\n78: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n83: ## Phase 3: Verification\n84: \n85: - [ ] T027 Run the agents-md check (`$S/after-check.txt`). Verify: `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK`, A4 `44 current`, A5 `31/31 pins hold`, A10 `6/6` and A6 at or under `16384`, expected `16092` with the T003 text unchanged.\n86: - [ ] T028 Run the rule-copy canary. Verify: `node .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/scripts/check-rule-copies.js | head -1` prints a line starting `OK: all rule invariants present`.\n87: - [ ] T029 Run the pointer test and check. Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed, and `node $SYNC --check` exits 0.\n88: - [ ] T030 Run the spec gate test. Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0`.\n89: - [ ] T031 Run the advisor checks. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -n \"copilot\" $ADV --glob \"*.ts\" --glob \"!dist/**\" --glob \"!node_modules/**\"` prints only the new test and the adapter-path guards in `tests/hooks/settings-driven-invocation-parity.vitest.ts` and `stress-test/skill-advisor/hooks-parity-stress.vitest.ts` and `npm test` reports 0 failed.\n90: - [ ] T032 Run the three hub checks. Verify: `for h in sk-doc sk-design system-deep-loop; do node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/$h > /dev/null 2>&1; echo \"$h exit=$?\"; done` prints `exit=0` three times.\n91: - [ ] T033 Rebuild the advisor and probe the hook. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run build` exits 0. Then `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"disable comment hygiene gate\"` prints a line holding `/doctor:git hooks (parent-named only)`, and the same command without the variable prints the phase 005 line with its policy word.\n92: - [ ] T034 Check scope and comment hygiene. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat` names only files in `spec.md` section 3, and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 -- '*.ts' '*.cjs' '*.mjs' '*.sh' | rg \"^\\+.*(REQ-0|T0[0-9]{2}|specs/|ADR-)\"` prints nothing.\n93: - [ ] T035 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n99: ## Completion Criteria\n100: \n101: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n102: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n103: - [ ] `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK` and `node $SYNC --check` exits 0 with the bullet in place\n104: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n109: ## Cross-References\n110: \n111: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n112: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n113: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n114: - **Review**: `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md` R5, R6, R10b, L4, L5, L10, G1 and G3\n115: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: ## Verification Checklist\n120: \n121: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n122: ## Verification Protocol\n123: \n124: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n125: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n126: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n127: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n128: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n129: \n130: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. An A6 reading above 16384 blocks the phase.\n131: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n132: \n133: ---\n134: \n135: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n136: ## Pre-Implementation\n137: \n138: - [x] CHK-001 [P0] The four wording questions have an operator answer, quoted in `spec.md` section 10. Evidence: answered on 2026-11-12 through the question dialog. T003, T006, T012, T013, T015 and T026 follow those answers.\n139: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The before numbers are in `$S/before.txt` (T001).\n140: - [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Phase 005's brief line is confirmed, or the REQ-004 tasks are marked `[B]` (T002).\n141: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n146: ## Code Quality\n147: \n148: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] In `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, and `node --check` exits 0 on `SYNC` and `spec-gate-core.mjs`.\n149: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a requirement or a task id (T034).\n150: - [ ] CHK-012 [P1] `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` is written by `SYNC` only, never by hand (T025).\n151: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The child branch reads the class, never the policy word alone (T015, T023).\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n157: ## Testing Checklist\n158: \n159: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK` with A6 at or under 16384 (T027).\n160: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The pointer test passes 7 cases and `--check` exits 0 (T029).\n161: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The child render test covers every renderer axis in `plan.md` (T023).\n162: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The spec gate test, the parity test and `npm test` in `$ADV` report 0 failed (T030, T031).\n163: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n164: \n165: ---\n166: \n167: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n168: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n169: \n170: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `cross-consumer`: one rule, read by seven runtimes through four surfaces.\n171: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the pointer generator is checked: `rg -l \"sync-gate1-pointers\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists only files this phase changed or confirmed unchanged in `plan.md`.\n172: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Every reader of `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` is checked: `rg -n \"GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE\" .skilled --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists the core, its test and the injection contract, which names it without quoting it.\n173: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The matrix axes in `plan.md` are listed in the two test file headers.\n174: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The child test sets and restores `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, so no other test sees it.\n175: - [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n176: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n177: \n178: ---\n179: \n180: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n181: ## Security\n182: \n183: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] A child never sees a bare `start` or `ask` command line (T023).\n184: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No changed file names `/local-skilled-alignment`: `rg -n \"local-skilled-alignment\" <changed files>` prints nothing.\n185: - [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The pointer block copies tracked `AGENTS.md` text only (T004).\n186: - [ ] CHK-033 [P0] A stored record carrying `copilot` is skipped by both readers without an error, and tool input carrying it is rejected (T022).\n187: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n188: \n189: ---\n190: \n191: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n192: ## Documentation\n193: \n194: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same bullet text, byte count and pin count.\n195: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] `HOOKDOC` names seven adapters and holds the invocation table (T005, T018).\n196: - [ ] CHK-042 [P2] The runtime-mirrors README names both pointer blocks (T021).\n197: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n198: \n199: ---\n200: \n201: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n202: ## File Organization\n203: \n204: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, before and after output live in `scratch/` only.\n205: - [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` holds only the evidence files the summary cites at completion.\n206: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n207: \n208: ---\n209: \n210: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n211: ## Verification Summary\n212: \n213: | Category | Total | Verified |\n214: |----------|-------|----------|\n215: | P0 Items | 13 | 1/13 |\n216: | P1 Items | 12 | 0/12 |\n217: | P2 Items | 1 | 0/1 |\n218: \n219: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-12\n220: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n221: \n222: ---"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794531672251,"end":1794531672284}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794531674254,"sessionID":"ses_e2d947600ffedS5gf0ax58bCAA","part":{"id":"prt_1d26c488e001D6wJ9RCbMpocSg","sessionID":"ses_e2d947600ffedS5gf0ax58bCAA","messageID":"msg_1d26c38b90010ayxkEK6fXxMOu","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"0531eea532078ba4842b2899dc9310419cd8f84d","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":680,"output":114,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":16768,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794531676422,"sessionID":"ses_e2d947600ffedS5gf0ax58bCAA","part":{"id":"prt_1d26c5106001eni1BlBlui4Aqu","sessionID":"ses_e2d947600ffedS5gf0ax58bCAA","messageID":"msg_1d26c4893001dSXeFQe40n2Yyy","type":"step-start","snapshot":"2c193182065ecb8a9e47b1f4c766868ce989b305"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794531681117,"sessionID":"ses_e2d947600ffedS5gf0ax58bCAA","part":{"partID":"prt_1d26c61c9002K48duJ7YxddMeG","sessionID":"ses_e2d947600ffedS5gf0ax58bCAA","messageID":"msg_1d26c4893001dSXeFQe40n2Yyy","type":"tool","id":"call_45e98b5c63d54833bfdba81f","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md, lines 1-521\n1: ---\n2: title: sk-doc Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n3: description: First-class surface router document at the sk-doc hub root (ROUTER.md). hub-router.json selects the workflow mode; this doc maps a request's documentation/authoring intent to the exact packet-local leaf resources that mode should load, emitting canonical (workflowMode, leafResourceId) pairs. Relocated verbatim from shared/references/smart-routing.md (v1.0.0.0) as the ROUTER.md consolidation pattern.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"sk-doc surface router\"\n6:   - \"doc authoring resource map\"\n7:   - \"packet leaf resource routing\"\n8:   - \"surface router pattern\"\n9: importance_tier: important\n10: contextType: implementation\n11: version: 2.4.5.0\n12: router_state: active\n13: skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # sk-doc Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n17: \n18: The machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). `SKILL.md` keeps the short routing prose and the link that points here; this file holds the declaration a reader parses to decide what loads.\n19: \n20: ---\n21: \n22: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n23: \n24: This is sk-doc's second-layer (surface) router, first-class at the hub root as\n25: `ROUTER.md`. The hub selects a workflow mode in [`hub-router.json`](hub-router.json)\n26: (sk-create-skill, sk-create-skill-parent, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command,\n27: sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark,\n28: sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter,\n29: sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, or sk-create-quality-control);\n30: this doc maps a request's documentation/authoring intent to the exact packet-local\n31: leaf resources that mode should load. Every path is either packet-qualified\n32: (`<packet>/references|assets/…`) or an authored shared-alias disk path (`shared/…`),\n33: and both convert to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at the\n34: contract boundary (`sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/lib/leaf-resource-contract.cjs`).\n35: `FULL_INVENTORY` is the single explicit full-toolkit intent — no other intent\n36: enumerates the whole hub.\n37: \n38: Routing is two stages: the hub picks the WORKFLOW mode (mode telemetry), this\n39: router picks the LEAVES within it. The two layers stay separate — the hub never\n40: emits leaf paths, and this router never re-decides the mode.\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 2. INTENT MODEL\n45: \n46: - **doc-quality leaves** — the validation rules, core standards, evergreen\n47:   packet-id rule, and the quality-control workflow a request to validate, audit,\n48:   or score documentation against sk-doc standards loads. Fired by \"documentation\n49:   quality / validate documentation / validate a document / score this document /\n50:   DQI / document audit / review the docs / document for clarity / audit the docs /\n51:   pass review\"\n52:   requests. The scoring phrases mirror `hub-router.json`, so a request that\n53:   reaches the quality mode at stage one also reaches its leaves at stage two.\n54: - **optimization leaves** — the optimization reference and the llms.txt templates\n55:   a request to compress, trim, or token-optimize a doc, or emit a machine-readable\n56:   index loads. Fired by \"optimize / token efficiency / llms.txt / reduce tokens /\n57:   slim down\" requests.\n58: - **skill-creation leaves** — the skill creation workflow and the skill.md /\n59:   readme / reference templates a request to scaffold or author a new skill loads.\n60:   Fired by \"create a skill / skill.md scaffold / resource_map wiring / package a\n61:   capability\" requests.\n62: - **parent-hub leaves.** The nested-packet contract, the hub-router schema and\n63:   the four parent-hub templates a request to build or rewire a parent hub loads.\n64:   Fired by \"parent hub / parent skill / mode packet / nested workflow packet /\n65:   mode-registry.json / hub-router.json\" requests, the file names spelled in full\n66:   so a bare \"hub router\" in an unrelated sentence does not fire it. This is the leaf set for the\n67:   `sk-create-skill-parent` mode, which shares the `sk-create-skill` packet but\n68:   not its leaves: a plain skill request must not pull the hub templates.\n69: - **render-ledger leaves.** The validation reference that explains the render\n70:   ledger's debt, exempt and pinned records and the doc rewrite guard, and the\n71:   maintenance workflow that runs the guard before a rewrite is committed. Fired\n72:   by \"doc rewrite guard / render ledger / render-known-debt.json / exempt from\n73:   the render checks / kept every claim\" requests. It belongs to the\n74:   `sk-create-skill` mode, which owns the ledger.\n75: - **agent-creation leaves.** The agent README and agent template a request to\n76:   scaffold an OpenCode agent loads. Fired by \"create an agent / new agent /\n77:   agent frontmatter / permission object / @analyze agent\" requests.\n78: - **command-creation leaves.** The command README and command template a\n79:   request to scaffold a slash command loads. Fired by \"create a command / slash\n80:   command / argument-hint / allowed-tools / thin router\" requests.\n81: - **agent-command leaves.** Both packets' READMEs and templates a request to\n82:   author an agent together with its paired `/create` command loads. Fired only\n83:   by the two paired phrases, \"agent and paired\" and \"paired /create\", which no\n84:   single-artifact request carries. The paired intent stays separate rather than\n85:   being expressed as the union of the two above, because the router keeps only\n86:   intents within one point of the top score: a paired request that also names\n87:   the agent would otherwise drop the command half.\n88: - **diagram and chart leaves belong to the `sk-design` hub.** ASCII flowchart,\n89:   decision-tree and standalone HTML chart authoring is `sk-design-diagram` and\n90:   `sk-design-chart` work, and this router declares no intent for it: `/design:diagram`\n91:   and `/design:chart` are the entry points, so \"flowchart\", \"ascii\", \"process diagram\",\n92:   \"create a chart\" and \"plot the data\" reach no key in the two maps below.\n93: - **human-voice leaves** — the scope gate, the scoring method and the Human\n94:   Voice Rules standard a request to apply or score that standard loads. Fired\n95:   by \"hvr / human voice rules / apply human voice / rewrite in human voice /\n96:   make this sound human / sounds ai-generated / remove ai tells\" requests. The\n97:   scope gate is the always-loaded leaf, because deciding what a voice edit may\n98:   touch comes before deciding what to change.\n99: - **playbook leaves** — the manual-testing-playbook README a request to author a\n100:   manual testing playbook loads. Fired by \"playbook system / manual testing\n101:   playbook / testing playbook / playbook scenario / manual test\n102:   scenario\" requests.\n103: - **playbook-conversation leaves** — the conversation-scenario reference and the\n104:   conversation snippet template a request to write a multi-turn json conversation script for\n105:   a playbook scenario loads. Fired by \"playbook conversation / multi-turn\n106:   conversation script / json conversation / conversation runner\" requests. This\n107:   intent scores double. \"manual testing playbook\" also matches \"testing\n108:   playbook\", so that one phrase scores the playbook intent twice, and at equal\n109:   weight a request naming both a playbook and a conversation would load only the\n110:   playbook README. At double weight the two tie and both leaf sets load.\n111: - **feature-catalog leaves** — the feature-catalog README a request to inventory a\n112:   project's features / capabilities loads. Fired by \"feature catalog / feature\n113:   inventory / capabilities\" requests.\n114: - **readme-creation leaves** — the readme README and readme template a request to\n115:   author a project README / front-page overview loads. Fired by \"create a readme /\n116:   readme for / project overview / landing doc\" requests.\n117: - **changelog leaves** — the changelog template a request to author release notes\n118:   / version notes loads. Fired by \"changelog / release notes / what shipped /\n119:   since the last version\" requests.\n120: - **benchmark leaves** — the benchmark shared README, worked example, and report\n121:   template a request to author a behavior benchmark\n122:   loads. Fired by \"create a benchmark / benchmark suite / behavior benchmark\"\n123:   requests.\n124: - **diff leaves** — the diff README, workflow, and worked example a request to\n125:   produce a before/after document diff loads. Fired by \"document diff / before\n126:   and after diff / visual document diff\" requests.\n127: - **repo-rule leaves** — the four decision tests, the rule anatomy contract, the\n128:   creation standards, the wiring contract, the rule and router templates, and the\n129:   packet reference map a\n130:   request to add, change, or remove a repo-local rule loads. Fired by \"repo rule /\n131:   project rule / REPO RULES.md / trigger table / retire a repo rule\" requests. Most such\n132:   requests end in a refusal, so `decision-tests.md` is the always-loaded leaf.\n133: - **frontmatter leaves** — the field reference and the versioning standard a\n134:   request about a frontmatter block itself loads. Fired by \"yaml frontmatter /\n135:   frontmatter block / frontmatter field / description budget / 4-part version /\n136:   frontmatter versioning\" requests. The phrases are qualified rather than bare,\n137:   because `agent frontmatter` belongs to agent-creation and a bare \"frontmatter\"\n138:   would take that route away from it. The field reference is the always-loaded\n139:   leaf, because resolving the document class comes before any field rule.\n140: - **goal-authoring leaves** — the goal authoring standards, the goal exemplars,\n141:   the parent/nested goal workflows and the budget/handoff reference a request to\n142:   author or revise a packet's `goal.md` loads. Fired by \"packet goal / goal.md /\n143:   goal document / author goal.md / phase parent goal / goal criteria /\n144:   completion checks\" requests. The phrases are qualified rather than bare,\n145:   because a bare \"goal\" and the session verbs belong to session-goal management\n146:   (set, bind, update, resend), which the goal hooks and host commands own. The\n147:   authoring standards are the always-loaded leaf, because what a goal must state\n148:   comes before how one is phrased.\n149: - **full-inventory leaves** — the entire sk-doc toolkit. `FULL_INVENTORY` is the\n150:   single explicit full-toolkit intent; no other intent enumerates the whole hub.\n151:   Fired only by an explicit \"show the full sk-doc toolkit / everything sk-doc\n152:   offers\" request.\n153: \n154: A single dominant documentation axis routes to one mode's leaf set; two clearly\n155: separate axes route to both.\n156: \n157: ---\n158: \n159: ## 3. MACHINE-READABLE ROUTER (replay / benchmark source)\n160: \n161: The single machine-readable projection of the intent model above. The prose is the\n162: human-facing contract; this block is the byte-for-byte source the deterministic\n163: router-replay parses. Keep them in sync: when a map row changes above, update the\n164: matching `RESOURCE_MAP` entry here. Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves on disk and\n165: dual-reads to a canonical typed pair through `leaf-manifest.json` or the hub's\n166: `leaf-aliases.json`.\n167: \n168: ```python\n169: INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n170:     \"DOC_QUALITY\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"documentation quality\", \"doc quality\", \"validate documentation\", \"validate a document\", \"validate this document\", \"validate markdown\", \"validation rules\", \"score this document\", \"score this doc\", \"dqi\", \"document audit\", \"fail sk-doc standards\", \"review the docs\", \"review the documentation\", \"document for clarity\", \"check the docs\", \"check the documentation\", \"audit the docs\", \"documentation review bar\", \"quality bar\", \"flag\", \"meet our standards\", \"audit documentation quality\", \"ai-friendly documentation\", \"extract structure\", \"validate\", \"score\", \"harden\", \"audit\", \"/doc:quality\"]},\n171:     \"OPTIMIZATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"optimize\", \"token efficiency\", \"llms.txt\", \"llmstxt\", \"reduce tokens\", \"fewer tokens\", \"trim\", \"compress the doc\", \"slim down\", \"model's budget\", \"machine-readable index\", \"optimize this doc\"]},\n172:     \"SKILL_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"sk-skill\", \"create a new sk\", \"create sk-\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"skill.md and starter\", \"resource_map wiring\", \"new skill\", \"create a skill\", \"build a skill\", \"author a skill\", \"scaffold a skill\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"new capability\", \"capability module\", \"package a capability\", \"create skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"package skill\", \"which json files does a skill need\", \"skill root metadata contract\", \"leaf-manifest config aliases required\", \"/create:skill\"]},\n173:     \"PARENT_HUB\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"parent hub\", \"parent skill\", \"mode packet\", \"mode packets\", \"nested packet\", \"nested workflow packet\", \"mode-registry.json\", \"hub-router.json\", \"hub versus standalone skill class\", \"skill hub\", \"/create:skill-parent\"]},\n174:     \"RENDER_LEDGER\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"rewrite guard\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n175:     \"AGENT_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create an agent\", \"create agent\", \"new agent\", \"author an agent\", \"scaffold an agent\", \"agent file\", \"agent persona\", \"agent frontmatter\", \"agent template\", \"permission object\", \"authority boundary\", \"@analyze agent\", \"opencode agent\", \"claude code agent\", \"/create:agent\"]},\n176:     \"COMMAND_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a command\", \"create command\", \"slash command\", \"new slash command\", \"author a command\", \"scaffold a command\", \"argument-hint\", \"allowed-tools\", \"command template\", \"router presentation split\", \"thin router\", \"presentation contract\", \"opencode command\", \"$arguments\", \"/create:command\"]},\n177:     \"AGENT_COMMAND\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"agent and paired\", \"paired /create\"]},\n178:     \"HVR\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"hvr\", \"human voice rules\", \"apply human voice\", \"rewrite in human voice\", \"make this sound human\", \"sounds ai-generated\", \"reads like ai wrote it\", \"reads like a machine wrote it\", \"remove ai tells\", \"ai writing tells\", \"voice pass\", \"de-ai the writing\", \"banned word check\", \"human voice\"]},\n179:     \"PLAYBOOK\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"playbook system\", \"manual testing playbook\", \"testing playbook\", \"deterministic scenario\", \"evidence collection\", \"operator validation\", \"multi-agent execution\", \"release readiness\", \"playbook scenario\", \"manual test scenario\", \"/create:manual-testing-playbook\"]},\n180:     \"PLAYBOOK_CONVERSATION\": {\"weight\": 8, \"keywords\": [\"playbook conversation\", \"multi-turn conversation script\", \"json conversation\", \"conversation runner\", \"run-conversation-scenario\"]},\n181:     \"FEATURE_CATALOG\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"feature catalog\", \"feature inventory\", \"catalog of features\", \"features overview\", \"capabilities\", \"catalog package\", \"per-feature files\", \"source anchors\", \"root catalog\", \"capability inventory\", \"/create:feature-catalog\"]},\n182:     \"README_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a readme\", \"readme for\", \"a readme\", \"front-page overview\", \"project overview\", \"getting started doc\", \"intro doc\", \"overview doc\", \"landing doc\", \"create readme\", \"readme\", \"folder readme\", \"write readme\", \"readme.md\", \"code folder readme\", \"/create:readme\"]},\n183:     \"CHANGELOG\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"changelog\", \"release notes\", \"version notes\", \"release summary\", \"what shipped\", \"since the last version\", \"changelog entry\", \"nested changelog\", \"packet changelog\", \"packet-local changelog\", \"create changelog\", \"global changelog\", \"vx.y.z.b\", \"/create:changelog\"]},\n184:     \"BENCHMARK\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a benchmark\", \"author a benchmark\", \"benchmark suite\", \"benchmark authoring\", \"behavior benchmark\", \"benchmark-report.md\", \"source.md\", \"mcp-server/benchmarks\", \"behavior-benchmark.md\", \"scenario contract\", \"claude-baseline\", \"benchmark/readme.md\", \"run-label folder\", \"benchmark package\", \"benchmark fixture\", \"benchmark profile\", \"reviewer-prompt fixture\", \"agent quality dimensions\", \"new benchmark\", \"promote benchmark folder\", \"create benchmark\", \"behavior_benchmark\"]},\n185:     \"DIFF\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"document diff\", \"doc diff\", \"diff document\", \"before and after diff\", \"before/after diff\", \"visual document diff\", \"create diff report\", \"document before after review\", \"before after document diff\", \"document change report\", \"before and after document\", \"document before/after review\", \"before/after document diff\", \"review document edits\", \"docx diff\", \"pdf diff\"]},\n186:     \"REPO_RULE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"repo rule\", \"repo-rules\", \"repo rules\", \"project rule\", \"repo rule file\", \"REPO RULES.md\", \"trigger table\", \"rule router\", \"retire a rule\", \"retire a repo rule\", \"revise a rule\", \"revise a repo rule\", \"add a repo rule\", \"always-loaded rule\", \"rule that binds\", \"create repo rule\", \"new repo rule\", \"repo-local rule\", \"we should always\", \"stop doing\", \"add a rule\", \"/create:repo-rule\"]},\n187:     \"FRONTMATTER\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"yaml frontmatter\", \"frontmatter block\", \"frontmatter template\", \"frontmatter field\", \"frontmatter fields\", \"trigger_phrases\", \"trigger phrases\", \"importance_tier\", \"contextType\", \"description budget\", \"4-part version\", \"X.Y.Z.W\", \"frontmatter versioning\", \"frontmatter version\", \"version field\", \"frontmatter validation\", \"missing frontmatter\", \"frontmatter contract\", \"yaml header\", \"goes at the top of the file\", \"version number at the top\", \"importance tier\", \"versioning pass\", \"stopped showing up in suggestions\", \"validator says my file is missing\", \"description too long\", \"edit count\", \"field the validator wants\"]},\n188:     \"GOAL_AUTHORING\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create packet goal\", \"packet goal\", \"goal.md\", \"author goal.md\", \"revise packet goal\", \"phase parent goal\", \"nested phase child goal\", \"nested goal\", \"add a goal file\", \"write a goal file\", \"draft a goal file\", \"goal file\", \"goal document\", \"goal criteria\", \"completion checks\", \"measurable criteria\", \"durable objective\", \"phase objective\", \"parent objective\", \"objective for a packet\", \"phase-child goal\", \"child-phase goal\", \"binding table\", \"goal chat slice\", \"/create:goal\"]},\n189:     \"FULL_INVENTORY\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"full sk-doc toolkit\", \"all templates\", \"entire toolkit\", \"everything sk-doc offers\"]},\n190: }\n191: \n192: RESOURCE_MAP = {\n193:     \"DOC_QUALITY\": [\n194:         \"shared/references/validation.md\",\n195:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/workflows.md\",\n196:         \"shared/references/core-standards.md\",\n197:         \"shared/references/evergreen-packet-id-rule.md\"\n198:     ],\n199:     \"OPTIMIZATION\": [\n200:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/optimization.md\",\n201:         \"shared/assets/llmstxt-templates.md\"\n202:     ],\n203:     \"SKILL_CREATION\": [\n204:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/creation-workflow.md\",\n205:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-md-template.md\",\n206:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-readme-template.md\",\n207:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md\"\n208:     ],\n209:     \"RENDER_LEDGER\": [\n210:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md\",\n211:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md\"\n212:     ],\n213:     \"PARENT_HUB\": [\n214:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md\",\n215:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md\",\n216:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md\",\n217:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-registry-template.json\",\n218:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-router-template.json\",\n219:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md\"\n220:     ],\n221:     \"AGENT_CREATION\": [\n222:         \"sk-create-agent/references/README.md\",\n223:         \"sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md\"\n224:     ],\n225:     \"COMMAND_CREATION\": [\n226:         \"sk-create-command/references/README.md\",\n227:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md\"\n228:     ],\n229:     \"AGENT_COMMAND\": [\n230:         \"sk-create-agent/references/README.md\",\n231:         \"sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md\",\n232:         \"sk-create-command/references/README.md\",\n233:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md\"\n234:     ],\n235:     \"HVR\": [\n236:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scope-and-exemptions.md\",\n237:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scoring-and-verification.md\",\n238:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/assets/voice-report-template.md\",\n239:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/hvr-rules.md\"\n240:     ],\n241:     \"PLAYBOOK\": [\n242:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/README.md\"\n243:     ],\n244:     \"PLAYBOOK_CONVERSATION\": [\n245:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/conversation-scenarios.md\",\n246:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/assets/manual-testing-playbook-conversation-snippet-template.md\"\n247:     ],\n248:     \"FEATURE_CATALOG\": [\n249:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/references/README.md\"\n250:     ],\n251:     \"README_CREATION\": [\n252:         \"sk-create-readme/references/README.md\",\n253:         \"sk-create-readme/assets/readme-template.md\"\n254:     ],\n255:     \"CHANGELOG\": [\n256:         \"sk-create-changelog/assets/changelog-template.md\"\n257:     ],\n258:     \"BENCHMARK\": [\n259:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/README.md\",\n260:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/worked-example.md\",\n261:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/shared/benchmark-report-template.md\"\n262:     ],\n263:     \"DIFF\": [\n264:         \"sk-create-diff/references/README.md\",\n265:         \"sk-create-diff/references/workflow.md\",\n266:         \"sk-create-diff/references/worked-example.md\"\n267:     ],\n268:     \"REPO_RULE\": [\n269:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/decision-tests.md\",\n270:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/rule-anatomy.md\",\n271:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/creation-standards.md\",\n272:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/agents-md-integration.md\",\n273:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rule-template.md\",\n274:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rules-router-template.md\",\n275:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/README.md\"\n276:     ],\n277:     \"FRONTMATTER\": [\n278:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-templates.md\",\n279:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/frontmatter-versioning.md\",\n280:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/README.md\"\n281:     ],\n282:     \"GOAL_AUTHORING\": [\n283:         \"sk-create-goal/references/authoring-standards.md\",\n284:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-exemplars.md\",\n285:         \"sk-create-goal/references/parent-and-nested-goals.md\",\n286:         \"sk-create-goal/references/budget-and-handoff.md\",\n287:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-top-level-template.md\",\n288:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-parent-template.md\",\n289:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-child-template.md\"\n290:     ],\n291:     \"FULL_INVENTORY\": [\n292:         \"sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md\",\n293:         \"sk-create-agent/references/README.md\",\n294:         \"sk-create-agent/references/agent-vs-skill-vs-command.md\",\n295:         \"sk-create-agent/references/common-pitfalls.md\",\n296:         \"sk-create-agent/references/permission-design.md\",\n297:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/fixtures/README.md\",\n298:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/fixtures/over-budget-description.md\",\n299:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/fixtures/under-budget-trim-lost-tokens.md\",\n300:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-templates.md\",\n301:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/README.md\",\n302:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/frontmatter-versioning.md\",\n303:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-exemplars.md\",\n304:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-child-template.md\",\n305:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-parent-template.md\",\n306:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-top-level-template.md\",\n307:         \"sk-create-goal/references/authoring-standards.md\",\n308:         \"sk-create-goal/references/budget-and-handoff.md\",\n309:         \"sk-create-goal/references/parent-and-nested-goals.md\",\n310:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-baseline-template.md\",\n311:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-index-template.md\",\n312:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-scenario-template.md\",\n313:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/shared/benchmark-report-template.md\",\n314:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/shared/source-template.md\",\n315:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-guide.md\",\n316:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/README.md\",\n317:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/case-studies.md\",\n318:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/pitfalls.md\",\n319:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/worked-example.md\",\n320:         \"sk-create-changelog/assets/changelog-template.md\",\n321:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/README.md\",\n322:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/topology-edge-cases.md\",\n323:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/version-bump-rules.md\",\n324:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/worked-examples.md\",\n325:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-contract.json\",\n326:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-contract.schema.json\",\n327:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-presentation-template.md\",\n328:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-router-template.md\",\n329:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md\",\n330:         \"sk-create-command/references/README.md\",\n331:         \"sk-create-command/references/argument-hints-and-modes.md\",\n332:         \"sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md\",\n333:         \"sk-create-command/references/router-presentation-split.md\",\n334:         \"sk-create-command/references/worked-example.md\",\n335:         \"sk-create-diff/assets/fixtures/README.md\",\n336:         \"sk-create-diff/assets/fixtures/onboarding-after.md\",\n337:         \"sk-create-diff/assets/fixtures/onboarding-before.md\",\n338:         \"sk-create-diff/references/README.md\",\n339:         \"sk-create-diff/references/accessibility-contract.md\",\n340:         \"sk-create-diff/references/capabilities-and-fidelity.md\",\n341:         \"sk-create-diff/references/cli-reference.md\",\n342:         \"sk-create-diff/references/worked-example.md\",\n343:         \"sk-create-diff/references/workflow.md\",\n344:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/assets/feature-catalog-snippet-template.md\",\n345:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/assets/feature-catalog-template.md\",\n346:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/references/README.md\",\n347:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/references/common-pitfalls.md\",\n348:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/references/examples.md\",\n349:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/assets/manual-testing-playbook-conversation-snippet-template.md\",\n350:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/assets/manual-testing-playbook-snippet-template.md\",\n351:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/assets/manual-testing-playbook-template.md\",\n352:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/README.md\",\n353:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/common-pitfalls.md\",\n354:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/conversation-scenarios.md\",\n355:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/examples.md\",\n356:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/prompt-voice.md\",\n357:         \"shared/assets/llmstxt-templates.md\",\n358:         \"shared/references/core-standards.md\",\n359:         \"shared/references/evergreen-packet-id-rule.md\",\n360:         \"shared/references/validation.md\",\n361:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/README.md\",\n362:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/optimization.md\",\n363:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/transformation-patterns.md\",\n364:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/validation-and-enforcement.md\",\n365:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/workflow-examples.md\",\n366:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/workflows.md\",\n367:         \"sk-create-readme/assets/architecture-template.md\",\n368:         \"sk-create-readme/assets/readme-code-template.md\",\n369:         \"sk-create-readme/assets/readme-template.md\",\n370:         \"sk-create-readme/references/README.md\",\n371:         \"sk-create-readme/references/readme/quality-and-checklist.md\",\n372:         \"sk-create-readme/references/readme/types-and-voice.md\",\n373:         \"sk-create-readme/references/readme/writing-patterns.md\",\n374:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rule-template.md\",\n375:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rules-router-template.md\",\n376:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/README.md\",\n377:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/agents-md-integration.md\",\n378:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/creation-standards.md\",\n379:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/decision-tests.md\",\n380:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/rule-anatomy.md\",\n381:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/assets/voice-report-template.md\",\n382:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/README.md\",\n383:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/hvr-rules.md\",\n384:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scope-and-exemptions.md\",\n385:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scoring-and-verification.md\",\n386:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-command-metadata-template.json\",\n387:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-description-template.json\",\n388:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-graph-metadata-template.json\",\n389:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-router-template.json\",\n390:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md\",\n391:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-leaf-aliases-template.json\",\n392:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md\",\n393:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-registry-template.json\",\n394:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md\",\n395:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/scaffold/hub-skill-scaffold.md\",\n396:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/scaffold/packet-skill-scaffold.md\",\n397:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md\",\n398:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-graph-metadata-template.json\",\n399:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-leaf-manifest-config-template.json\",\n400:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-md-template.md\",\n401:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md\",\n402:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-readme-template.md\",\n403:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md\",\n404:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md\",\n405:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md\",\n406:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md\",\n407:         \"sk-create-skill/references/README.md\",\n408:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-architecture.md\",\n409:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-lockstep-surfaces.json\",\n410:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md\",\n411:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md\",\n412:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\",\n413:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/common-pitfalls.md\",\n414:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/overview.md\",\n415:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md\",\n416:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md\",\n417:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/creation-workflow.md\",\n418:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md\",\n419:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md\"\n420:     ],\n421: }\n422: ```\n423: \n424: ---\n425: \n426: ## 4. HOW TO READ THIS\n427: \n428: - One dominant intent routes to one mode's leaf set.\n429: - Two near-tied intents (within the ambiguity delta) route to both leaf sets; the\n430:   union is deduped by canonical pair.\n431: - No keyword match is UNKNOWN_FALLBACK: confirm the target artifact and intent\n432:   before loading anything.\n433: - `FULL_INVENTORY` fires only on an explicit \"show the whole toolkit\" request.\n434: \n435: ---\n436: \n437: ## 5. MACHINE ROUTER\n438: \n439: The hub's detailed routing prose, moved here from `SKILL.md` so the skill body keeps only a short routing summary and a pointer to this file. It sits last, after the stage-two map above, and it declares no map of its own: the `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` block in section 3 stays the only replay source.\n440: \n441: > **Compiled routing (default-on, flag-gated, additive).** Resolve the mode via the compiled router contract first:\n442: > ```bash\n443: > node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt \"<task>\"\n444: > ```\n445: > Follow the returned decision — `route` (use its `targets`), `clarify`/`defer` (disambiguate), `reject` (refuse). On a `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}` sentinel or any error, use the routing below. The front door self-gates on serving-authority. Compiled routing is now the default for `sk-doc`; set `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=0` to force legacy routing fleet-wide — the explicit kill-switch.\n446: \n447: ### Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n448: \n449: Stage 2 of routing lives in section 3 of this file.\n450: It defines three things:\n451: - The per-intent leaf model: document quality, optimization, skill creation, parent-hub creation, agent creation, command creation, the paired agent-plus-command lane, the human-voice pass, playbooks, playbook conversations, feature catalogs, READMEs, changelogs, benchmarks, diffs, frontmatter, packet goals, repo rules, and the explicit full-toolkit intent.\n452: - The machine-readable `INTENT_SIGNALS` / `RESOURCE_MAP` block that the deterministic router-replay and benchmarks parse.\n453: - The how-to-read rules: a dominant intent gives one leaf set, near-tied intents give a deduped union, and no keyword match gives the hub UNKNOWN fallback, never a silent default.\n454: \n455: Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path is packet-qualified or an authored shared-alias disk path, and each converts to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at the one contract boundary.\n456: \n457: The reason this file stays a separate document from `SKILL.md` and from `hub-router.json` is in [the parent-skill reference](sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md#why-the-leaf-router-stays-in-routermd).\n458: \n459: ### The discriminator\n460: - **`workflowMode`** — the public packet key (e.g. `sk-create-skill`, `sk-create-quality-control`). `sk-create-skill-parent` is a second mode over the same `sk-create-skill` packet.\n461: - **`packetKind`** — `workflow` for every sk-doc packet (there is no surface axis; the sk-create-quality-control pipeline is universal doctrine in `shared/`, not orthogonal stack-evidence).\n462: - **`backendKind`** — `template-scaffold` for the create-* generators, `sk-create-quality-control` for the sk-create-quality-control mode.\n463: \n464: ### Routing rule\n465: ```\n466: SKILL_ROOT = path containing this ROUTER.md and its SKILL.md\n467: REGISTRY = SKILL_ROOT / \"mode-registry.json\"\n468: HUB_ROUTER = SKILL_ROOT / \"hub-router.json\"\n469: \n470: UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n471:     \"Confirm whether this is sk-create-skill, sk-create-skill-parent, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command, sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark, sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter, sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, or sk-create-quality-control work\",\n472:     \"Confirm the target document or component being authored, scaffolded, or reviewed\",\n473:     \"Provide the available inputs: existing doc, source material, or scaffold parameters\",\n474:     \"Confirm the validation expectations before completion (DQI/HVR scoring, validate.sh, or packet-specific checks)\",\n475: ]\n476: \n477: def _guard_in_skill(relative_path):\n478:   resolved = (SKILL_ROOT / relative_path).resolve()\n479:   resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT)\n480:   if resolved.suffix.lower() not in {\".md\", \".json\"}:\n481:     raise ValueError(\"only skill-local markdown/json router resources are routable\")\n482:   return resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix()\n483: \n484: def load_if_available(relative_path, seen):\n485:   guarded = _guard_in_skill(relative_path)\n486:   if guarded not in seen and (SKILL_ROOT / guarded).exists():\n487:     load(guarded)\n488:     seen.add(guarded)\n489:     return True\n490:   return False\n491: \n492: seen = set()\n493: if not REGISTRY.exists() or not HUB_ROUTER.exists():\n494:   return defer(\"router metadata missing; inspect sk-doc/mode-registry.json and sk-doc/hub-router.json\")\n495: \n496: read mode-registry.json and hub-router.json\n497: classify the request to one or more workflowMode values using hub-router.json\n498:   (dominant authoring/quality intent; a command like /create:agent resolves directly)\n499: \n500: if confidence is low, intent is contradictory, or routerPolicy.defaultMode is null and no mode wins:\n501:   for resource in hub_router.routerPolicy.defaultResource:   # the ordered defer set, never hardcoded here\n502:     load_if_available(resource, seen)\n503:   return UNKNOWN_FALLBACK with disambiguation_checklist = UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST\n504: \n505: for each resolved workflowMode:\n506:   entry = the matching mode-registry.json modes[] item\n507:   if entry is missing or entry.packetKind != \"workflow\":\n508:     return defer(\"unknown sk-doc workflowMode; extend mode-registry.json and create a packet first\")\n509:   if not load_if_available(f\"{entry.packet}/SKILL.md\", seen):\n510:     return defer(\"registered packet SKILL.md is missing; repair the packet before routing\")\n511: \n512: return single or orderedBundle according to hub-router.json routerPolicy.outcomes\n513: ```\n514: `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`: an unclear documentation intent asks for disambiguation rather than forcing a stale default. `hub-router.json` carries the router signals, vocabulary classes, default fallback resource, and bundle rules. Outcomes are `single`, `orderedBundle`, or `defer` — there is no `surfaceBundle` (no surface axis).\n515: \n516: Per-packet behavior is **not flattened**: each packet keeps its own authoring contract, references, assets, scripts, and templates.\n517: \n518: This hub does **not** use keyed resource discovery (`references/<key>/` or `assets/<key>/`) at the hub root.\n519: There are no hub-root `references/` or `assets/` directories, and packet resources stay inside their owning packet or the shared backbone.\n520: If a future workflow needs keyed resource subdirectories, add that behavior inside the owning packet using guarded runtime discovery.\n521: Do not hardcode resource inventories in this hub.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md, lines 1-521\n1: ---\n2: title: sk-doc Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n3: description: First-class surface router document at the sk-doc hub root (ROUTER.md). hub-router.json selects the workflow mode; this doc maps a request's documentation/authoring intent to the exact packet-local leaf resources that mode should load, emitting canonical (workflowMode, leafResourceId) pairs. Relocated verbatim from shared/references/smart-routing.md (v1.0.0.0) as the ROUTER.md consolidation pattern.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"sk-doc surface router\"\n6:   - \"doc authoring resource map\"\n7:   - \"packet leaf resource routing\"\n8:   - \"surface router pattern\"\n9: importance_tier: important\n10: contextType: implementation\n11: version: 2.4.5.0\n12: router_state: active\n13: skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # sk-doc Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n17: \n18: The machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). `SKILL.md` keeps the short routing prose and the link that points here; this file holds the declaration a reader parses to decide what loads.\n19: \n20: ---\n21: \n22: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n23: \n24: This is sk-doc's second-layer (surface) router, first-class at the hub root as\n25: `ROUTER.md`. The hub selects a workflow mode in [`hub-router.json`](hub-router.json)\n26: (sk-create-skill, sk-create-skill-parent, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command,\n27: sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark,\n28: sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter,\n29: sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, or sk-create-quality-control);\n30: this doc maps a request's documentation/authoring intent to the exact packet-local\n31: leaf resources that mode should load. Every path is either packet-qualified\n32: (`<packet>/references|assets/…`) or an authored shared-alias disk path (`shared/…`),\n33: and both convert to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at the\n34: contract boundary (`sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/lib/leaf-resource-contract.cjs`).\n35: `FULL_INVENTORY` is the single explicit full-toolkit intent — no other intent\n36: enumerates the whole hub.\n37: \n38: Routing is two stages: the hub picks the WORKFLOW mode (mode telemetry), this\n39: router picks the LEAVES within it. The two layers stay separate — the hub never\n40: emits leaf paths, and this router never re-decides the mode.\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 2. INTENT MODEL\n45: \n46: - **doc-quality leaves** — the validation rules, core standards, evergreen\n47:   packet-id rule, and the quality-control workflow a request to validate, audit,\n48:   or score documentation against sk-doc standards loads. Fired by \"documentation\n49:   quality / validate documentation / validate a document / score this document /\n50:   DQI / document audit / review the docs / document for clarity / audit the docs /\n51:   pass review\"\n52:   requests. The scoring phrases mirror `hub-router.json`, so a request that\n53:   reaches the quality mode at stage one also reaches its leaves at stage two.\n54: - **optimization leaves** — the optimization reference and the llms.txt templates\n55:   a request to compress, trim, or token-optimize a doc, or emit a machine-readable\n56:   index loads. Fired by \"optimize / token efficiency / llms.txt / reduce tokens /\n57:   slim down\" requests.\n58: - **skill-creation leaves** — the skill creation workflow and the skill.md /\n59:   readme / reference templates a request to scaffold or author a new skill loads.\n60:   Fired by \"create a skill / skill.md scaffold / resource_map wiring / package a\n61:   capability\" requests.\n62: - **parent-hub leaves.** The nested-packet contract, the hub-router schema and\n63:   the four parent-hub templates a request to build or rewire a parent hub loads.\n64:   Fired by \"parent hub / parent skill / mode packet / nested workflow packet /\n65:   mode-registry.json / hub-router.json\" requests, the file names spelled in full\n66:   so a bare \"hub router\" in an unrelated sentence does not fire it. This is the leaf set for the\n67:   `sk-create-skill-parent` mode, which shares the `sk-create-skill` packet but\n68:   not its leaves: a plain skill request must not pull the hub templates.\n69: - **render-ledger leaves.** The validation reference that explains the render\n70:   ledger's debt, exempt and pinned records and the doc rewrite guard, and the\n71:   maintenance workflow that runs the guard before a rewrite is committed. Fired\n72:   by \"doc rewrite guard / render ledger / render-known-debt.json / exempt from\n73:   the render checks / kept every claim\" requests. It belongs to the\n74:   `sk-create-skill` mode, which owns the ledger.\n75: - **agent-creation leaves.** The agent README and agent template a request to\n76:   scaffold an OpenCode agent loads. Fired by \"create an agent / new agent /\n77:   agent frontmatter / permission object / @analyze agent\" requests.\n78: - **command-creation leaves.** The command README and command template a\n79:   request to scaffold a slash command loads. Fired by \"create a command / slash\n80:   command / argument-hint / allowed-tools / thin router\" requests.\n81: - **agent-command leaves.** Both packets' READMEs and templates a request to\n82:   author an agent together with its paired `/create` command loads. Fired only\n83:   by the two paired phrases, \"agent and paired\" and \"paired /create\", which no\n84:   single-artifact request carries. The paired intent stays separate rather than\n85:   being expressed as the union of the two above, because the router keeps only\n86:   intents within one point of the top score: a paired request that also names\n87:   the agent would otherwise drop the command half.\n88: - **diagram and chart leaves belong to the `sk-design` hub.** ASCII flowchart,\n89:   decision-tree and standalone HTML chart authoring is `sk-design-diagram` and\n90:   `sk-design-chart` work, and this router declares no intent for it: `/design:diagram`\n91:   and `/design:chart` are the entry points, so \"flowchart\", \"ascii\", \"process diagram\",\n92:   \"create a chart\" and \"plot the data\" reach no key in the two maps below.\n93: - **human-voice leaves** — the scope gate, the scoring method and the Human\n94:   Voice Rules standard a request to apply or score that standard loads. Fired\n95:   by \"hvr / human voice rules / apply human voice / rewrite in human voice /\n96:   make this sound human / sounds ai-generated / remove ai tells\" requests. The\n97:   scope gate is the always-loaded leaf, because deciding what a voice edit may\n98:   touch comes before deciding what to change.\n99: - **playbook leaves** — the manual-testing-playbook README a request to author a\n100:   manual testing playbook loads. Fired by \"playbook system / manual testing\n101:   playbook / testing playbook / playbook scenario / manual test\n102:   scenario\" requests.\n103: - **playbook-conversation leaves** — the conversation-scenario reference and the\n104:   conversation snippet template a request to write a multi-turn json conversation script for\n105:   a playbook scenario loads. Fired by \"playbook conversation / multi-turn\n106:   conversation script / json conversation / conversation runner\" requests. This\n107:   intent scores double. \"manual testing playbook\" also matches \"testing\n108:   playbook\", so that one phrase scores the playbook intent twice, and at equal\n109:   weight a request naming both a playbook and a conversation would load only the\n110:   playbook README. At double weight the two tie and both leaf sets load.\n111: - **feature-catalog leaves** — the feature-catalog README a request to inventory a\n112:   project's features / capabilities loads. Fired by \"feature catalog / feature\n113:   inventory / capabilities\" requests.\n114: - **readme-creation leaves** — the readme README and readme template a request to\n115:   author a project README / front-page overview loads. Fired by \"create a readme /\n116:   readme for / project overview / landing doc\" requests.\n117: - **changelog leaves** — the changelog template a request to author release notes\n118:   / version notes loads. Fired by \"changelog / release notes / what shipped /\n119:   since the last version\" requests.\n120: - **benchmark leaves** — the benchmark shared README, worked example, and report\n121:   template a request to author a behavior benchmark\n122:   loads. Fired by \"create a benchmark / benchmark suite / behavior benchmark\"\n123:   requests.\n124: - **diff leaves** — the diff README, workflow, and worked example a request to\n125:   produce a before/after document diff loads. Fired by \"document diff / before\n126:   and after diff / visual document diff\" requests.\n127: - **repo-rule leaves** — the four decision tests, the rule anatomy contract, the\n128:   creation standards, the wiring contract, the rule and router templates, and the\n129:   packet reference map a\n130:   request to add, change, or remove a repo-local rule loads. Fired by \"repo rule /\n131:   project rule / REPO RULES.md / trigger table / retire a repo rule\" requests. Most such\n132:   requests end in a refusal, so `decision-tests.md` is the always-loaded leaf.\n133: - **frontmatter leaves** — the field reference and the versioning standard a\n134:   request about a frontmatter block itself loads. Fired by \"yaml frontmatter /\n135:   frontmatter block / frontmatter field / description budget / 4-part version /\n136:   frontmatter versioning\" requests. The phrases are qualified rather than bare,\n137:   because `agent frontmatter` belongs to agent-creation and a bare \"frontmatter\"\n138:   would take that route away from it. The field reference is the always-loaded\n139:   leaf, because resolving the document class comes before any field rule.\n140: - **goal-authoring leaves** — the goal authoring standards, the goal exemplars,\n141:   the parent/nested goal workflows and the budget/handoff reference a request to\n142:   author or revise a packet's `goal.md` loads. Fired by \"packet goal / goal.md /\n143:   goal document / author goal.md / phase parent goal / goal criteria /\n144:   completion checks\" requests. The phrases are qualified rather than bare,\n145:   because a bare \"goal\" and the session verbs belong to session-goal management\n146:   (set, bind, update, resend), which the goal hooks and host commands own. The\n147:   authoring standards are the always-loaded leaf, because what a goal must state\n148:   comes before how one is phrased.\n149: - **full-inventory leaves** — the entire sk-doc toolkit. `FULL_INVENTORY` is the\n150:   single explicit full-toolkit intent; no other intent enumerates the whole hub.\n151:   Fired only by an explicit \"show the full sk-doc toolkit / everything sk-doc\n152:   offers\" request.\n153: \n154: A single dominant documentation axis routes to one mode's leaf set; two clearly\n155: separate axes route to both.\n156: \n157: ---\n158: \n159: ## 3. MACHINE-READABLE ROUTER (replay / benchmark source)\n160: \n161: The single machine-readable projection of the intent model above. The prose is the\n162: human-facing contract; this block is the byte-for-byte source the deterministic\n163: router-replay parses. Keep them in sync: when a map row changes above, update the\n164: matching `RESOURCE_MAP` entry here. Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves on disk and\n165: dual-reads to a canonical typed pair through `leaf-manifest.json` or the hub's\n166: `leaf-aliases.json`.\n167: \n168: ```python\n169: INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n170:     \"DOC_QUALITY\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"documentation quality\", \"doc quality\", \"validate documentation\", \"validate a document\", \"validate this document\", \"validate markdown\", \"validation rules\", \"score this document\", \"score this doc\", \"dqi\", \"document audit\", \"fail sk-doc standards\", \"review the docs\", \"review the documentation\", \"document for clarity\", \"check the docs\", \"check the documentation\", \"audit the docs\", \"documentation review bar\", \"quality bar\", \"flag\", \"meet our standards\", \"audit documentation quality\", \"ai-friendly documentation\", \"extract structure\", \"validate\", \"score\", \"harden\", \"audit\", \"/doc:quality\"]},\n171:     \"OPTIMIZATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"optimize\", \"token efficiency\", \"llms.txt\", \"llmstxt\", \"reduce tokens\", \"fewer tokens\", \"trim\", \"compress the doc\", \"slim down\", \"model's budget\", \"machine-readable index\", \"optimize this doc\"]},\n172:     \"SKILL_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"sk-skill\", \"create a new sk\", \"create sk-\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"skill.md and starter\", \"resource_map wiring\", \"new skill\", \"create a skill\", \"build a skill\", \"author a skill\", \"scaffold a skill\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"new capability\", \"capability module\", \"package a capability\", \"create skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"package skill\", \"which json files does a skill need\", \"skill root metadata contract\", \"leaf-manifest config aliases required\", \"/create:skill\"]},\n173:     \"PARENT_HUB\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"parent hub\", \"parent skill\", \"mode packet\", \"mode packets\", \"nested packet\", \"nested workflow packet\", \"mode-registry.json\", \"hub-router.json\", \"hub versus standalone skill class\", \"skill hub\", \"/create:skill-parent\"]},\n174:     \"RENDER_LEDGER\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"rewrite guard\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n175:     \"AGENT_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create an agent\", \"create agent\", \"new agent\", \"author an agent\", \"scaffold an agent\", \"agent file\", \"agent persona\", \"agent frontmatter\", \"agent template\", \"permission object\", \"authority boundary\", \"@analyze agent\", \"opencode agent\", \"claude code agent\", \"/create:agent\"]},\n176:     \"COMMAND_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a command\", \"create command\", \"slash command\", \"new slash command\", \"author a command\", \"scaffold a command\", \"argument-hint\", \"allowed-tools\", \"command template\", \"router presentation split\", \"thin router\", \"presentation contract\", \"opencode command\", \"$arguments\", \"/create:command\"]},\n177:     \"AGENT_COMMAND\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"agent and paired\", \"paired /create\"]},\n178:     \"HVR\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"hvr\", \"human voice rules\", \"apply human voice\", \"rewrite in human voice\", \"make this sound human\", \"sounds ai-generated\", \"reads like ai wrote it\", \"reads like a machine wrote it\", \"remove ai tells\", \"ai writing tells\", \"voice pass\", \"de-ai the writing\", \"banned word check\", \"human voice\"]},\n179:     \"PLAYBOOK\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"playbook system\", \"manual testing playbook\", \"testing playbook\", \"deterministic scenario\", \"evidence collection\", \"operator validation\", \"multi-agent execution\", \"release readiness\", \"playbook scenario\", \"manual test scenario\", \"/create:manual-testing-playbook\"]},\n180:     \"PLAYBOOK_CONVERSATION\": {\"weight\": 8, \"keywords\": [\"playbook conversation\", \"multi-turn conversation script\", \"json conversation\", \"conversation runner\", \"run-conversation-scenario\"]},\n181:     \"FEATURE_CATALOG\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"feature catalog\", \"feature inventory\", \"catalog of features\", \"features overview\", \"capabilities\", \"catalog package\", \"per-feature files\", \"source anchors\", \"root catalog\", \"capability inventory\", \"/create:feature-catalog\"]},\n182:     \"README_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a readme\", \"readme for\", \"a readme\", \"front-page overview\", \"project overview\", \"getting started doc\", \"intro doc\", \"overview doc\", \"landing doc\", \"create readme\", \"readme\", \"folder readme\", \"write readme\", \"readme.md\", \"code folder readme\", \"/create:readme\"]},\n183:     \"CHANGELOG\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"changelog\", \"release notes\", \"version notes\", \"release summary\", \"what shipped\", \"since the last version\", \"changelog entry\", \"nested changelog\", \"packet changelog\", \"packet-local changelog\", \"create changelog\", \"global changelog\", \"vx.y.z.b\", \"/create:changelog\"]},\n184:     \"BENCHMARK\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a benchmark\", \"author a benchmark\", \"benchmark suite\", \"benchmark authoring\", \"behavior benchmark\", \"benchmark-report.md\", \"source.md\", \"mcp-server/benchmarks\", \"behavior-benchmark.md\", \"scenario contract\", \"claude-baseline\", \"benchmark/readme.md\", \"run-label folder\", \"benchmark package\", \"benchmark fixture\", \"benchmark profile\", \"reviewer-prompt fixture\", \"agent quality dimensions\", \"new benchmark\", \"promote benchmark folder\", \"create benchmark\", \"behavior_benchmark\"]},\n185:     \"DIFF\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"document diff\", \"doc diff\", \"diff document\", \"before and after diff\", \"before/after diff\", \"visual document diff\", \"create diff report\", \"document before after review\", \"before after document diff\", \"document change report\", \"before and after document\", \"document before/after review\", \"before/after document diff\", \"review document edits\", \"docx diff\", \"pdf diff\"]},\n186:     \"REPO_RULE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"repo rule\", \"repo-rules\", \"repo rules\", \"project rule\", \"repo rule file\", \"REPO RULES.md\", \"trigger table\", \"rule router\", \"retire a rule\", \"retire a repo rule\", \"revise a rule\", \"revise a repo rule\", \"add a repo rule\", \"always-loaded rule\", \"rule that binds\", \"create repo rule\", \"new repo rule\", \"repo-local rule\", \"we should always\", \"stop doing\", \"add a rule\", \"/create:repo-rule\"]},\n187:     \"FRONTMATTER\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"yaml frontmatter\", \"frontmatter block\", \"frontmatter template\", \"frontmatter field\", \"frontmatter fields\", \"trigger_phrases\", \"trigger phrases\", \"importance_tier\", \"contextType\", \"description budget\", \"4-part version\", \"X.Y.Z.W\", \"frontmatter versioning\", \"frontmatter version\", \"version field\", \"frontmatter validation\", \"missing frontmatter\", \"frontmatter contract\", \"yaml header\", \"goes at the top of the file\", \"version number at the top\", \"importance tier\", \"versioning pass\", \"stopped showing up in suggestions\", \"validator says my file is missing\", \"description too long\", \"edit count\", \"field the validator wants\"]},\n188:     \"GOAL_AUTHORING\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create packet goal\", \"packet goal\", \"goal.md\", \"author goal.md\", \"revise packet goal\", \"phase parent goal\", \"nested phase child goal\", \"nested goal\", \"add a goal file\", \"write a goal file\", \"draft a goal file\", \"goal file\", \"goal document\", \"goal criteria\", \"completion checks\", \"measurable criteria\", \"durable objective\", \"phase objective\", \"parent objective\", \"objective for a packet\", \"phase-child goal\", \"child-phase goal\", \"binding table\", \"goal chat slice\", \"/create:goal\"]},\n189:     \"FULL_INVENTORY\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"full sk-doc toolkit\", \"all templates\", \"entire toolkit\", \"everything sk-doc offers\"]},\n190: }\n191: \n192: RESOURCE_MAP = {\n193:     \"DOC_QUALITY\": [\n194:         \"shared/references/validation.md\",\n195:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/workflows.md\",\n196:         \"shared/references/core-standards.md\",\n197:         \"shared/references/evergreen-packet-id-rule.md\"\n198:     ],\n199:     \"OPTIMIZATION\": [\n200:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/optimization.md\",\n201:         \"shared/assets/llmstxt-templates.md\"\n202:     ],\n203:     \"SKILL_CREATION\": [\n204:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/creation-workflow.md\",\n205:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-md-template.md\",\n206:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-readme-template.md\",\n207:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md\"\n208:     ],\n209:     \"RENDER_LEDGER\": [\n210:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md\",\n211:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md\"\n212:     ],\n213:     \"PARENT_HUB\": [\n214:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md\",\n215:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md\",\n216:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md\",\n217:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-registry-template.json\",\n218:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-router-template.json\",\n219:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md\"\n220:     ],\n221:     \"AGENT_CREATION\": [\n222:         \"sk-create-agent/references/README.md\",\n223:         \"sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md\"\n224:     ],\n225:     \"COMMAND_CREATION\": [\n226:         \"sk-create-command/references/README.md\",\n227:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md\"\n228:     ],\n229:     \"AGENT_COMMAND\": [\n230:         \"sk-create-agent/references/README.md\",\n231:         \"sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md\",\n232:         \"sk-create-command/references/README.md\",\n233:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md\"\n234:     ],\n235:     \"HVR\": [\n236:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scope-and-exemptions.md\",\n237:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scoring-and-verification.md\",\n238:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/assets/voice-report-template.md\",\n239:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/hvr-rules.md\"\n240:     ],\n241:     \"PLAYBOOK\": [\n242:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/README.md\"\n243:     ],\n244:     \"PLAYBOOK_CONVERSATION\": [\n245:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/conversation-scenarios.md\",\n246:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/assets/manual-testing-playbook-conversation-snippet-template.md\"\n247:     ],\n248:     \"FEATURE_CATALOG\": [\n249:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/references/README.md\"\n250:     ],\n251:     \"README_CREATION\": [\n252:         \"sk-create-readme/references/README.md\",\n253:         \"sk-create-readme/assets/readme-template.md\"\n254:     ],\n255:     \"CHANGELOG\": [\n256:         \"sk-create-changelog/assets/changelog-template.md\"\n257:     ],\n258:     \"BENCHMARK\": [\n259:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/README.md\",\n260:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/worked-example.md\",\n261:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/shared/benchmark-report-template.md\"\n262:     ],\n263:     \"DIFF\": [\n264:         \"sk-create-diff/references/README.md\",\n265:         \"sk-create-diff/references/workflow.md\",\n266:         \"sk-create-diff/references/worked-example.md\"\n267:     ],\n268:     \"REPO_RULE\": [\n269:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/decision-tests.md\",\n270:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/rule-anatomy.md\",\n271:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/creation-standards.md\",\n272:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/agents-md-integration.md\",\n273:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rule-template.md\",\n274:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rules-router-template.md\",\n275:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/README.md\"\n276:     ],\n277:     \"FRONTMATTER\": [\n278:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-templates.md\",\n279:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/frontmatter-versioning.md\",\n280:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/README.md\"\n281:     ],\n282:     \"GOAL_AUTHORING\": [\n283:         \"sk-create-goal/references/authoring-standards.md\",\n284:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-exemplars.md\",\n285:         \"sk-create-goal/references/parent-and-nested-goals.md\",\n286:         \"sk-create-goal/references/budget-and-handoff.md\",\n287:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-top-level-template.md\",\n288:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-parent-template.md\",\n289:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-child-template.md\"\n290:     ],\n291:     \"FULL_INVENTORY\": [\n292:         \"sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md\",\n293:         \"sk-create-agent/references/README.md\",\n294:         \"sk-create-agent/references/agent-vs-skill-vs-command.md\",\n295:         \"sk-create-agent/references/common-pitfalls.md\",\n296:         \"sk-create-agent/references/permission-design.md\",\n297:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/fixtures/README.md\",\n298:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/fixtures/over-budget-description.md\",\n299:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/fixtures/under-budget-trim-lost-tokens.md\",\n300:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-templates.md\",\n301:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/README.md\",\n302:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/frontmatter-versioning.md\",\n303:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-exemplars.md\",\n304:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-child-template.md\",\n305:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-parent-template.md\",\n306:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-top-level-template.md\",\n307:         \"sk-create-goal/references/authoring-standards.md\",\n308:         \"sk-create-goal/references/budget-and-handoff.md\",\n309:         \"sk-create-goal/references/parent-and-nested-goals.md\",\n310:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-baseline-template.md\",\n311:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-index-template.md\",\n312:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-scenario-template.md\",\n313:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/shared/benchmark-report-template.md\",\n314:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/shared/source-template.md\",\n315:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-guide.md\",\n316:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/README.md\",\n317:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/case-studies.md\",\n318:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/pitfalls.md\",\n319:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/worked-example.md\",\n320:         \"sk-create-changelog/assets/changelog-template.md\",\n321:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/README.md\",\n322:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/topology-edge-cases.md\",\n323:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/version-bump-rules.md\",\n324:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/worked-examples.md\",\n325:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-contract.json\",\n326:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-contract.schema.json\",\n327:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-presentation-template.md\",\n328:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-router-template.md\",\n329:         \"sk-cr